\begin{align*}
f'(x) &= 1 - \frac{56}{(x - 8)^2} \\
&= \frac{(x - 8)^2 - 56}{(x - 8)^2} \\
&= \frac{x^2 - 16x + 32}{(x - 8)^2} \\
&= \frac{x^2 - 16x + 64 - 32}{(x - 8)^2} \\
&= \frac{(x - 8)^2 - 32}{(x - 8)^2} \\
&= \frac{(\sqrt{32} - x + 8)(-\sqrt{32} - x + 8)}{(x - 8)^2}.
\end{align*}Thus, $f(x)$ has a minimum value at either $x = 8 + \sqrt{32} = 8 + 4 \sqrt{2}$ or $x = 8 - \sqrt{32} = 8 - 4\sqrt{2}.$  Since $x > 8,$ $x = 8 + 4 \sqrt{2}.$

Then the minimum value of $f(x)$ is
